## Gotchas checklist

### Audio / WAV
- [ ] Compositions play **WAV**, not MP3 (the repeat-at-start trap).
- [ ] `start_time` is `N/A`/zero on all WAVs (`ffprobe` to confirm).
- [ ] Track shape matches audio layout (per-act vs single continuous).
- [ ] Cold open `chapterIntroFrames=0`; all other acts `120`.
- [ ] WAVs **mastered** (Step 0g) to ~-14 LUFS / -1 dBTP transparent, with `durΔ < 0.01s` per act verified BEFORE swapping (mastering must not move timing).
- [ ] WAVs covered by Git LFS before committing.

### TTS path (skip if audio was given)
- [ ] Script edited for speech flow before chunking (staccato fragments merged, list periods → semicolons, very short paragraphs merged).
- [ ] Decide the path: **prosody-free** (ep4 — `**`/`[停顿]` inert) vs **prosody** (#13 — `**`→audio emphasis, `[停顿]`→baked silence). Use `tts-wittgenstein.js` as the template for the prosody path.
- [ ] `**bold**` handling matches the chosen path (inert-and-stripped, or split-into-prosody-segments-then-stripped-for-display).
- [ ] `[停顿]` / `[长停顿]` handling matches the chosen path (inert, or forced chunk boundary + baked trailing silence ~180ms/450ms).
- [ ] NO inline `<prosody>` SSML in the `text` arg — it is spoken literally. Use the MCP's `rate`/`pitch`/`volume` params (whole-utterance) + per-segment splitting for intra-sentence variation.
- [ ] Prosody path: `parseSegments()` merges punctuation-only segments into a neighbor (avoids "No audio was received"); TTS calls wrapped in a retry.
- [ ] Prosody path: inner segment joins trimmed tight THEN given a contextual `joinBeat` (~0.32s before a reveal, ~0.26s after ——/：) so setup→reveal beats aren't crushed. Verify with `ffmpeg silencedetect` (~0.39s at a reveal join).
- [ ] No bare Latin initials in spoken prose (e.g. "早期W") — TTS reads them as letters; write the full name.
- [ ] Every polyphonic character in key terms has a `PRONUNCIATION_SUBS` entry — `ttsText` uses the substitute, `displayText` uses the original.
- [ ] Pronunciation substitutions reversed in `CONTEXTUAL_FOLDS` (so the alignment cursor matches the narration's original characters; fold BOTH the substitute char and any homophone Whisper emits for it, e.g. 属数/熟熟→数数).
- [ ] Chunk manifest `chunks.json` saved per act (enables surgical regeneration).
- [ ] WAV `start_time=N/A` confirmed after concat (not just assumed).
- [ ] Inserted beats/silence GROW act durations — after any prosody/beat edit, re-run concat → transcribe → build, and re-sync `AUDIO_LEN_SEC`.

### Build-subs script
- [ ] Section heading lookup uses `normalizeHeading()` (curly quotes trap).
- [ ] `processBlock()` strips `**...**` before building display text.
- [ ] Frame geometry in the build script matches the project frame (1440 vs 1920).
- [ ] Auto-emphasis only if narration is plain; tag-driven if it has `[强调]`.
- [ ] Every spoken numeral has a CONTEXTUAL_FOLDS entry; longer patterns first.
- [ ] Traditional→simplified `SAFE_FOLDS` map present if Whisper drifted (human audio).
- [ ] Homophone folds seeded for inanimate `它→他` phrases + any 集/级, 合上/和尚-class same-sound mishearings (the silent cursor-jump trap). On a many-male-referent script (维特根斯坦/塞尔/哈纳德…) NEVER add a bare `他→它` — use the LONGEST specific phrase fold, and verify the wrong form is absent from the narration first.
- [ ] Classical/idiom quotes folded if Whisper homophones them (#13: 得意忘言→德意妄言, 王弼→王毕, 荀粲→荀灿, 得鱼而忘筌→得鱼而忘全).
- [ ] Display-only strips (em dashes) applied to `c.text` AFTER alignment but BEFORE `autoTagEmphases` (no audio/timing impact; only the build step re-runs).
- [ ] **Monotonic sweep clean on EVERY act** — `nonmono:0 degen:0`, no >6.5s single chunks (catches the homophone cursor-jump trap that fires no warning).
- [ ] Chunk counts per act verified after building (zero chunks = silent heading mismatch).
- [ ] Never hand-edit `{actId}.subs.ts` — edit narration/tables, regenerate.

### STT timing integrity
- [ ] `words.json` `durationSec` ≈ true WAV duration on EVERY act (gap >1.5s = Whisper tail-truncation; splice the final chunk's standalone transcription).
- [ ] Tail-splice script computes `OFFSET = ffdur(actWav) − ffdur(finalChunkMp3)` DYNAMICALLY (do NOT hardcode — durations shift every regeneration; a stale offset silently mis-times the spliced tail).
- [ ] Tail-truncation can recur after a regen (it's format/length-driven, not random) — re-check + re-splice after every full regenerate, then rebuild.
- [ ] After any re-transcribe or tail-splice, `AUDIO_LEN_SEC[actId]` in `acts.ts` re-synced to the new `durationSec`.

### Generated assets (gpt-image-2 plates / cutouts)
- [ ] Each installed asset matches its spec's **dimensions + aspect** (portrait plate is 1024×1536, not a landscape variant).
- [ ] Register B parchment plates carry **NO magenta** (composited as documents); only Register A cutouts use `#FF00FF` chroma-key + `cutout-bg.js`.
- [ ] The file copied into `assets/` is the CORRECT generation — when a batch produces several variants in `out/`, verify the installed one (dimensions, background, layout) rather than assuming.

### Remotion project
- [ ] `AUDIO_LEN_SEC` in `acts.ts` populated from `words.json` `durationSec` values.
- [ ] All act compositions registered in `Root.tsx` with correct durations.
- [ ] `npx tsc --noEmit` clean (deprecation warnings OK, type errors not).
- [ ] `npx remotion compositions` lists all expected IDs with correct durations.
- [ ] Still render at a mid-act frame confirms terrain + particles + subtitles render.
- [ ] Temp still PNG cleaned up after verification.
